# {{ project_slug }}

Streaming Delta Pipeline (DLT) implementing bronze → silver → gold over the Databricks TPCH sample dataset, deployed as a Databricks Asset Bundle.

## Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) v0.230+, authenticated (`databricks auth login`)
- A Unity Catalog-enabled workspace with access to `samples.tpch`
- Permission to create catalogs in the metastore — the bundle creates the `bronze_catalog`, `silver_catalog`, and `gold_catalog` (see Variables below) and the schemas within them

## What's here

```
src/pipelines/
├── bronze/ingest.py           # Streaming ingestion from samples.tpch (one @dp.table per source)
├── silver/                    # Data-quality expectations + CDC (SCD Type 1) into cleansed tables
└── gold/                      # Materialized views: dim_customer, dim_part, dim_supplier, fact_order
                                # (surrogate keys via xxhash64 on the natural key)
resources/
├── pipelines/pipeline.yml     # DLT pipeline resource (serverless, ADVANCED edition)
└── schemas/schemas.yml        # Bronze/silver/gold UC schema declarations
```

Silver tables enforce data-quality expectations (e.g. `@dp.expect("non_negative_balance", ...)`) on a streaming view, then apply changes into a target table via `dp.create_auto_cdc_flow` (SCD Type 1). Gold builds materialized views on top of silver with a surrogate key column derived from the natural key.

## Deploy

Set your workspace URLs in `databricks.yml` under each target, then:

```bash
databricks bundle validate --target dev
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
```

The pipeline appears under **Delta Live Tables** in the Databricks UI — start it from there, or set a schedule in `resources/pipelines/pipeline.yml`.

For production:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --target prod
```

## Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `bronze_catalog` | `dpa_sdp_bronze_dev` | Catalog for raw ingested data |
| `silver_catalog` | `dpa_sdp_silver_dev` | Catalog for cleansed and validated data |
| `gold_catalog` | `dpa_sdp_gold_dev` | Catalog for the dimensional model |

Override at deploy time:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy \
  --var="bronze_catalog=my_bronze" \
  --var="silver_catalog=my_silver" \
  --var="gold_catalog=my_gold"
```

## Troubleshooting

- **"Metastore storage root URL does not exist"** — your metastore doesn't have default storage configured, so the bundle can't create the target catalogs automatically. Either enable default storage for the metastore (account console → Unity Catalog), or create one catalog manually via the UI first to provision the storage root, then redeploy.
- **Pipeline fails on first run** — confirm the workspace has access to `samples.tpch` (bundled with every Databricks workspace by default).
